{"id":"fat","name":"Fat","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:fat"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Fat","text":"(Heb. heleb) denotes the richest part of the animal, or the fattest of the flock, in the account of Abel’s sacrifice (Gen. 4:4). It sometimes denotes the best of any production (Gen. 45:18; Num. 18:12; Ps. 81:16; 147:47). The fat of sacrifices was to be burned (Lev. 3:9-11; 4:8; 7:3; 8:25; Num. 18:17. Comp. Ex. 29:13-22; Lev. 3:3-5). It is used figuratively for a dull, stupid state of mind (Ps 17:10). In Joel 2:24 the word is equivalent to “vat,” a vessel. The hebrew word here thus rendered is elsewhere rendered “wine-fat” and “press-fat” (Hag. 2:16; Isa. 63:2)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2459","lemma":"חֶלֶב","xlit":"cheleb","gloss":"fat, whether literally or figuratively","kjv":"best, fat, finest, grease","count":27,"share":0.77},{"strong":"H3508","lemma":"יֹתֶרֶת","xlit":"yôthereth","gloss":"the lobe or flap of the liver","kjv":"caul","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H3516","lemma":"כָּבֵד","xlit":"kâbêd","gloss":"the liver","kjv":"liver","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H3629","lemma":"כִּלְיָה","xlit":"kilyâh","gloss":"a kidney","kjv":"kidneys, reins","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H6999","lemma":"קָטַר","xlit":"qâṭar","gloss":"to smoke","kjv":"burn, incense, kindle, offer","count":10,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H801","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","xlit":"ʼishshâh","gloss":"a burnt-offering","kjv":"by fire","count":8,"share":0.23}],"verses":["Gen.45.18","Exod.23.18","Exod.29.13","Exod.29.22","Lev.3.3","Lev.3.4","Lev.3.9","Lev.3.10","Lev.3.14","Lev.3.15","Lev.3.16","Lev.3.17","Lev.4.8","Lev.4.9","Lev.7.3","Lev.7.4","Lev.7.23","Lev.8.16","Lev.8.25","Lev.8.26","Lev.10.15","Lev.17.6","Deut.32.38","1Sam.2.15","1Sam.2.16","Ps.81.16","Isa.43.24","Gen.49.20","Lev.1.8","Lev.3.5","Lev.3.11","Lev.4.10","Lev.7.5","Ps.37.20","Isa.25.6"],"related":[{"id":"caul","type":"cooccur","shared":9,"jaccard":0.237,"why":"9 verses are indexed un